  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: GSSAPI authentication state persisted across attempts\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-106555.patch: reset the global GSSAPI client\n       state at the start of each authentication request and GSSAPI context\n       setup, except for gssapi-keyex and post-authentication re-keying.\n     - CVE-2026-106555\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: GSSAPI credentials stored after failed authentication\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-106553.patch: only store delegated GSSAPI\n       credentials when the GSSAPI client was authorized.\n     - CVE-2026-106553\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: injection via command-line username\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-106583.patch: disallow '$' and '\\' in a\n       command-line supplied username.\n     - CVE-2026-106583",
